<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sakanoue no Tamuramaro</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">758–811</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sakanoue no Tamuramaro was a Japanese general and court noble of the early Heian period. Appointed seii taishōgun in 797, he led the campaigns against the Emishi of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honshu">Honshu</a>, built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isawa-castle">Isawa Castle</a> in 802 and received the surrender of the Emishi leader Aterui that year. He was later honoured as a model warrior, and tradition links him with the founding of the Kiyomizu-dera temple in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyoto">Kyoto</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sakanoue-no-tamuramaro.jpg" alt="Sakanoue no Tamuramaro" width="320" height="355" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sakanoue_Tamuramaro_sw.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
